Z||000000||Adrift||09-13-2001||12:29 AM||||I was watching a discussion on TV today between Tom Clancy and a whole group of other people, and a very interesting point was raised by an Israeli general. For the last twelve months North Americans (And the rest of the world) have been critizing Israel for assassinating Palestine generals which are involved in the planning and training of suicide bombers. Now the Americans, which have been unfortunately placed in the same situation, have responded in the same way (I believe bush's statement was along the lines of "We hold responsible not only those directly responsible for the attack but also those who might have helped hide those whom are directly responsible".)<P>Really made me rethink my opinion of the Israel situation. Could you imagine if there were suicide bombings in North America 1-3 times PER WEEK, and we KNEW exactly who they were and where they were coming from? We wouldn't even give "the enemy" (whomever it may be in this case, Ben Laden or whatever) a chance to beg!||||reg||1
